                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Brownsville TX",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued November 7 at 9:50PM CST until November 9 at 9:00AM CST by NWS Brownsville TX",
                "description": "Multiple rounds of locally heavy rainfall are expected through early\nMonday morning.  The first round is most likely between midnight and\nmid-morning Sunday, when 2 to 3 inches with locally 4 or more inches\nof rain may fall. The second round is expected Sunday night into\nearly Monday morning, when an additional 1 to 3 inches with locally 4\ninches or more possible.\n\n* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of Deep South Texas, including the following\ncounties, Brooks, Jim Hogg and Zapata.\n\n* WHEN...Through Monday morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nCreeks and streams may rise out of their banks. Flooding may occur\nin poor drainage and urban areas. Storm drains and ditches may\nbecome clogged with debris.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Potential for heavy rainfall, including two windows where\nrainfall rates could reach 2 inches per hour for two hours both\nlate tonight and early Sunday morning, and again Sunday night\nthrough mid morning Monday.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be alert for possible Flood\nWarnings. Those living in areas prone to flooding should be prepared\nto take action should flooding develop.",
